---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Residential Architect GTA | NV Studio Design"
  description="Residential architecture studio in the Greater Toronto Area. Custom homes, renovations, additions, and permit-ready drawings across Ontario. Book a consultation."
  keywords="residential architect GTA, residential architecture Toronto, custom home architect Ontario, home renovation architect GTA, laneway house designer Toronto"
  headerClass="alt"
>
  <section id="banner" slot="banner">
    <div class="inner">
      <header class="major">
        <h1>Residential Architecture Studio in the GTA</h1>
      </header>
      <div class="content">
        <p>
          Custom homes, renovations, and additions for homeowners and builders
          across the Greater Toronto Area and Ontario.
        </p>
        <ul class="actions">
          <li><a href={`${baseUrl}contact`} class="button primary">Book a Consultation</a></li>
          <li><a href={`${baseUrl}portfolio`} class="button">See Our Work</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="one">
    <div class="inner">
      <header class="major">
        <h2>Residential design, start to finish</h2>
      </header>
      <p>
        NV Studio Design is a residential architecture and interior design
        practice based in the Greater Toronto Area. We work with homeowners
        and small developers across the GTA and Ontario on custom homes,
        whole-house renovations, additions, and laneway suites &mdash; from the
        first zoning check through permit drawings and construction.
      </p>
      <p>
        We run design and permitting as <strong>one integrated process</strong>,
        not separate services. That means the feasibility, zoning review, and
        drawings a city reviewer expects are built into the design from day
        one &mdash; not bolted on at the end.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="two" class="alt">
    <div class="inner">
      <header class="major">
        <h2>Who we work with</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="row gtr-50 gtr-uniform">
        <div class="col-4 col-12-medium">
          <h3>Homeowners</h3>
          <p>
            Planning a new custom home, a significant renovation, or an addition
            in Toronto, Mississauga, Oakville, Vaughan, or the surrounding GTA.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-4 col-12-medium">
          <h3>Builders &amp; small developers</h3>
          <p>
            Need permit-ready residential drawings, zoning reviews, or a design
            partner who can coordinate with your trades and consultants.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-4 col-12-medium">
          <h3>Property owners exploring what&rsquo;s possible</h3>
          <p>
            Not sure whether your lot supports what you have in mind? A short
            feasibility and zoning review is often the right first step.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="three">
    <div class="inner">
      <header class="major">
        <h2>Services</h2>
      </header>
      <p>
        Three services, one practice. Every residential project we take on
        moves through some combination of the three &mdash; coordinated end to
        end so nothing falls between handoffs.
      </p>
      <div class="row gtr-50 gtr-uniform">
        <div class="col-4 col-12-medium">
          <article class="project-card">
            <header class="major">
              <h3><a href={`${baseUrl}architectural-design`}>Architectural Design</a></h3>
            </header>
            <p>
              Concept, design development, and construction documents for
              custom homes, renovations, and additions &mdash; with zoning
              review and permits folded in.
            </p>
            <ul class="actions">
              <li><a href={`${baseUrl}architectural-design`} class="button">Learn more</a></li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="col-4 col-12-medium">
          <article class="project-card">
            <header class="major">
              <h3><a href={`${baseUrl}interior-design`}>Interior Design</a></h3>
            </header>
            <p>
              Residential interiors developed alongside the architecture:
              space planning, materials and finishes, built-ins, kitchens,
              and bathrooms.
            </p>
            <ul class="actions">
              <li><a href={`${baseUrl}interior-design`} class="button">Learn more</a></li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="col-4 col-12-medium">
          <article class="project-card">
            <header class="major">
              <h3><a href={`${baseUrl}building-permits`}>Planning &amp; Permits</a></h3>
            </header>
            <p>
              Zoning review, feasibility studies, and permit drawings for
              Ontario municipalities &mdash; including additions, secondary
              suites, and laneway houses.
            </p>
            <ul class="actions">
              <li><a href={`${baseUrl}building-permits`} class="button">Learn more</a></li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="four" class="alt">
    <div class="inner">
      <header class="major">
        <h2>Selected projects</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="row gtr-50 gtr-uniform">
        <div class="col-4 col-12-medium">
          <article class="project-card">
            <a href={`${baseUrl}project-modern-residential-villa`} class="image">
              <img
                src="images/projects/modern-residential-villa/1-m5KLpxQggBCWDKl6.jpg"
                alt="Modern residential villa &mdash; contemporary custom home by NV Studio Design, Greater Toronto Area"
              />
            </a>
            <header class="major">
              <h3><a href={`${baseUrl}project-modern-residential-villa`}>Modern Residential Villa</a></h3>
              <p>Custom home &middot; Greater Toronto Area</p>
            </header>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="col-4 col-12-medium">
          <article class="project-card">
            <a href={`${baseUrl}project-luxury-home-renovation`} class="image">
              <img
                src="images/projects/luxury-home-renovation/3-A3QOoKVygoIkW0VX.jpg"
                alt="Luxury whole-house renovation by NV Studio Design, Greater Toronto Area"
              />
            </a>
            <header class="major">
              <h3><a href={`${baseUrl}project-luxury-home-renovation`}>Luxury Home Renovation</a></h3>
              <p>Whole-house renovation &middot; GTA</p>
            </header>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="col-4 col-12-medium">
          <article class="project-card">
            <a href={`${baseUrl}project-laneway-house`} class="image">
              <img
                src="images/projects/laneway-house-project/1a-YD0ng4naVrtpzOMo.jpg"
                alt="Laneway house, 850 square feet, designed by NV Studio Design, Toronto"
              />
            </a>
            <header class="major">
              <h3><a href={`${baseUrl}project-laneway-house`}>Laneway House</a></h3>
              <p>Secondary dwelling &middot; Toronto</p>
            </header>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="actions">
        <li><a href={`${baseUrl}portfolio`} class="button">View full portfolio</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="five">
    <div class="inner">
      <header class="major">
        <h2>Why clients work with us</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="row gtr-50 gtr-uniform">
        <div class="col-6 col-12-medium">
          <h3>Residential focus</h3>
          <p>
            Houses are all we do. Every project in the portfolio is a home,
            a renovation, or a secondary suite &mdash; not commercial, not
            institutional.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-6 col-12-medium">
          <h3>GTA zoning &amp; permits</h3>
          <p>
            Toronto, Mississauga, Vaughan, Oakville, and neighbouring
            municipalities each apply by-laws differently. We design with
            those rules in mind from the first sketch.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-6 col-12-medium">
          <h3>Integrated design &amp; interiors</h3>
          <p>
            Architecture and interiors developed together, so cabinetry,
            lighting, and finishes resolve cleanly into the built form.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-6 col-12-medium">
          <h3>Clear communication</h3>
          <p>
            Honest timelines, plain-language updates, and drawings your
            builder can actually use on site.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="six" class="alt">
    <div class="inner">
      <header class="major">
        <h2>How a project moves</h2>
      </header>
      <p>
        Most residential projects pass through five phases. More detail on the
        <a href={`${baseUrl}process`}>Process</a> page.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Initial consultation &amp; site review</strong> &mdash; we talk through the brief, look at the site, and flag anything the lot or the by-law will constrain.</li>
        <li><strong>Concept &amp; feasibility</strong> &mdash; early sketches tested against zoning so you know what&rsquo;s actually buildable.</li>
        <li><strong>Design development</strong> &mdash; plans, elevations, and interior decisions resolved together.</li>
        <li><strong>Permit drawings &amp; approvals</strong> &mdash; a complete submission package and coordination with the city reviewer.</li>
        <li><strong>Construction coordination</strong> &mdash; answering the builder&rsquo;s questions and keeping the design intact on site.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="seven">
    <div class="inner">
      <header class="major">
        <h2>Planning a residential project in the GTA?</h2>
      </header>
      <p>
        A short consultation is the fastest way to find out whether your
        project is a good fit and what the realistic next step looks like.
      </p>
      <ul class="actions">
        <li><a href={`${baseUrl}contact`} class="button primary">Book a Consultation</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${baseUrl}about`} class="button">About the Studio</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
